# PsychoFlow — example environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. The demo runs end to end with none of it set:
#   venv/Scripts/python.exe sim/run_demo.py
# Every variable below unlocks an optional path, and each one fails closed
# rather than breaking the demo when it is absent.
#
# COMMIT THIS FILE. Never commit `.env` — it is gitignored for the obvious
# reason, and a key that reaches the history is a key that has to be rotated.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sarvam AI — SPEECH ONLY (§14, DESIGN.md §7.5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by BOTH `--stt sarvam` (Saarika/Saaras speech-to-text) and
# `--tts sarvam` (Bulbul, which speaks the confirmation line). One key covers
# both.
#
# WHAT IT IS ALLOWED TO DO: transcription and speech synthesis, nothing else.
# It is never in the reasoning path. Intent parsing — the only step that
# decides anything — is ALWAYS local Gemma via Ollama. There is no Claude API
# call and no paid inference anywhere in the runtime path, which is a budget
# constraint rather than a style preference.
#
# LEAVE IT BLANK unless you specifically want cloud STT. With no key the
# sarvam provider is simply UNAVAILABLE — not an error — and the default
# `--stt whisper` runs faster-whisper locally, needing no key and no network.
# That default exists so the demo survives conference wifi, and so nothing
# spends free-tier credit by accident: `sarvam` is reached only by typing it,
# and no test in this repo sets it.
#
# The key is read once at startup and is never logged, never returned by
# `/voice/status`, never placed on the §13.2 frame, and never written to the
# command log. Sarvam error paths deliberately keep the HTTP STATUS only and
# not the response body, so a key cannot escape through an error either.
SARVAM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard (Vite) — set in the FRONTEND environment, not the backend's
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `sim/run_demo.py` sets VITE_WS_URL for its frontend child automatically, so
# these are only needed when running `npm run dev` by hand. Without either, the
# dashboard plays the recorded session in `frontend/fixtures/` and needs no
# backend at all — the assistant then reads "offline parser" rather than
# pretending a local model answered.
#
# The assistant's HTTP origin is derived from VITE_WS_URL when VITE_API_URL is
# unset, so a dashboard pointed at a live corridor talks to that corridor.
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUMO
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for anything that runs the simulator. `sumolib`/`traci` resolve from
# $SUMO_HOME/tools, not from pip.
# SUMO_HOME=C:\Program Files (x86)\Eclipse\Sumo
